<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1901" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">al-lăbōro</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adl-</span></b> ), āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. (only twice in Hor.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to labor or toil
				at a thing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ore adlaborandum est tibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 8, 20</span></i>
			.—And with dat., <i>to add
				to with labor</i> or <i>pains</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simplici myrto nihil adlabores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 38, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
